From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:33:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 039/108] Exclude raylib from the Metal runtime backend

Select the Metal backend before configuring runtime dependencies. Skip raylib and the desktop debug UI, exclude legacy presentation and sample-audio calls, and use native keyboard action IDs directly. Preserve the non-Metal backend.

Verified with Tarzan integration: build; 56/56 CTest entries; VU generator tests; VU replay 1130 runs, 0 mismatches/rejected/skipped. First-mission baseline/candidate: 25.1/25.1 FPS, CPU user 152.342/151.802 s (-0.35%, within noise; no performance change established), CPU sys 2.380/2.360 s; 0 fallbacks, 0 steady underruns, no crash. Runner 88362363 -> 86914331 bytes; no raylib/GLFW/rlImGui/ImGui symbols or direct OpenGL/Carbon imports. Package audit clean.

